.TH WWW 1 "October 2026" "www 3.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
www \- simple static HTTP and HTTPS server
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B www
.RB [ \-p " port"]
.RB [ \-r " path"]
.RB [ \-q ]
.RB [ \-s " domain"]
.RB [ \-\-cert-cache " path"]
.RB [ \-\-acme-staging ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Serve the current directory on all interfaces, using HTTP port 8000 by default.
Directories serve index.html when present, otherwise a directory listing.
Files are streamed with HEAD, range, and conditional request support.
Hidden files are served and ordinary symbolic links are followed.
The active certificate cache and its aliases are excluded.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-p " port"
Listening port; default 8000. Domain HTTPS always uses 443.
.TP
.BI \-r " path"
Document root; default the current directory.
.TP
.B \-q
Suppress startup and request logs. Errors remain visible on standard error.
.TP
.BI \-s " domain"
Enable HTTPS. The exact name localhost creates a temporary self-signed certificate
and respects the selected port. Other DNS names use Let's Encrypt on port 443.
.TP
.BI \-\-cert-cache " path"
Override persistent ACME account and certificate storage. Requires domain HTTPS.
An existing directory must have owner-only permissions.
.TP
.B \-\-acme-staging
Use Let's Encrypt staging for testing. Requires domain HTTPS.
Staging certificates are not publicly trusted.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show help.
.TP
.B \-V
Show the package version.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Show the package version and full source commit hash.
Builds without source metadata show unknown instead of a hash.
.SH HTTPS
Point the domain's DNS A record to the server's public IPv4 address.
Publish an AAAA record only when public IPv6 reaches the same server.
Public TCP port 443 must reach www directly, with TLS intact.
TLS-ALPN-01 validation uses the HTTPS listener; port 80 is unnecessary.
The process needs permission to bind port 443.
Certificates are obtained and renewed while the server runs.
.SH FILES
On Linux and FreeBSD, ACME storage is $XDG_DATA_HOME/www/acme or
$HOME/.local/share/www/acme. On macOS it is
$HOME/Library/Application Support/io.nbari.www/acme.
New cache directories use mode 0700 and files use 0600 on Unix.
The older Go certificate cache is not imported.
.SH EXAMPLES
.B www \-r /tmp \-p 8080
.PP
.B www \-s localhost \-r ./public \-p 8080
.PP
.B www \-s share.example.com \-r ./public \-\-acme-staging
.PP
.B www \-s share.example.com \-r ./public
.SH SIGNALS
SIGINT and SIGTERM stop accepting connections and allow a bounded graceful drain.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Zero after a normal shutdown; nonzero on invalid arguments or fatal startup/runtime errors.
